From: Johan Alvarado <contact@c127.dev>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 22:40:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: ipq5018: enable smp2p ssr ack

The Q6 on IPQ5018 boots exactly once. Any later start - after a firmware
crash or after a plain stop/start - fails with:

  qcom-q6-mpd cd00000.remoteproc: start timed out
  remoteproc remoteproc0: can't start rproc cd00000.remoteproc: -110

qcom_scm_pas_auth_and_reset() returns 0 and the Q6 does come up: the
smp2p master interrupt fires during the failed start. What never arrives
is the "ready" edge, because the local side never acknowledges the
remote restart, so its cached entry values are stale and setting "ready"
again produces no transition.

This is the same problem 8devices fixed for IPQ6018 in "soc: qcom: fix
smp2p ack on ipq6018", which added qcom,smp2p-feature-ssr-ack to the
master-kernel node and made qcom_smp2p_intr() send the ack when that
property is present. The driver side already applies to every SoC; only
the IPQ6018 device tree ever opted in. IPQ5018 needs the same property,
and its smp2p node is otherwise identical.

Signed-off-by: Johan Alvarado <contact@c127.dev>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq5018.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq5018.dtsi
@@ -1212,6 +1212,7 @@
 
 		wcss_smp2p_out: master-kernel {
 			qcom,entry-name = "master-kernel";
+			qcom,smp2p-feature-ssr-ack;
 			#qcom,smem-state-cells = <1>;
 		};
 
